    "title": "pandas.PeriodIndex.second — pandas 3.1.0.dev0 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.PeriodIndex.second#\n\n- property PeriodIndex.second[source]#\n- The second of the period. Returns the second component for each period in the index. See also \n  - `PeriodIndex.hour`\n  - The hour of the period.\n  - `PeriodIndex.minute`\n  - The minute of the period.\n  - `PeriodIndex.to_timestamp`\n  - Cast to DatetimeArray/Index.\n Examples >>> idx = pd.PeriodIndex([\"2023-01-01 10:00:30\", ... \"2023-01-01 10:00:31\"], freq='s') >>> idx.second Index([30, 31], dtype='int64')",
    "markdown_length": 478,
